+/*
+ * Bring-up: printf, not the kprintf this macro used to be, and switchable.
+ * See the bootstrap-trace patch header.
+ *
+ * Switchable because this console has no scrollback and these forty-odd
+ * lines are the first thing a screenful of later output pushes off the top.
+ * They were worth having until the interesting output moved past them --
+ * fsck's complaint about the root volume arrives after bsd_init() is done
+ * and could not be read with the trace on. bsdtrace=0 turns it off.
+ *
+ * At file scope rather than inside bsd_init(), because bsdinit_task() uses
+ * the macro as well and a function-local static is not in scope there.
+ * bsd_init() reads the boot-arg into it and runs first; the -1 it starts at
+ * is truthy, so the default stays "on" whoever gets there first.
